[{:adr/authoritative_for ["isic-5820 dossier-canonical-id wiring" "MHLW licensed-agency registry investigation (confirmed, not pulled)"], :adr/topic "isic-5820-dossier-canonical-id-wiring-mhlw-investigation", :adr/related ["adr-2607182200" "adr-2607173400"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607182300-isic-5820-dossier-canonical-id-wiring", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-18", :adr/body "# ADR-2607182300: cloud-itonami-isic-5820 -- wire Account/Lead to the canonical dossier business-entity id\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-18\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (owner directive: \\\"1, 2\\\" -- MHLW licensed-agency registry investigation + dossier-canonical-id wiring into 5820, following ADR-2607182200)\n**Scope**: `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5820` (child commit `4f47230f4111`), west pin advance.\n\n## Part 1: MHLW licensed-agency registry (investigated, not yet pulled)\n\nConfirmed real and working: \u539a\u751f\u52b4\u50cd\u7701 (MHLW) \\\"\u4eba\u6750\u30b5\u30fc\u30d3\u30b9\u7dcf\u5408\u30b5\u30a4\u30c8\\\" (jinzai.hellowork.mhlw.go.jp) publishes a live, public search system for every licensed \u8077\u696d\u7d39\u4ecb\u4e8b\u696d\u8005 (employment placement agency) in Japan -- exactly cloud-itonami-isic-7810's target segment. A real query (Tokyo prefecture, no other filters) returned **12,008 real results** for Tokyo alone, each with \u8a31\u53ef\u30fb\u53d7\u7406\u756a\u53f7 (license number, e.g. \\\"01-\u30e6-300184\\\"), \u8a31\u53ef\u5e74\u6708\u65e5 (license date), \u4e8b\u696d\u4e3b\u6c0f\u540d/\u4e8b\u696d\u6240\u540d\u79f0 (legal business name / establishment name), \u4e8b\u696d\u6240\u6240\u5728\u5730/\u96fb\u8a71\u756a\u53f7 (business address / phone -- government-disclosed for transparency, not personal data). The form is a session-based Struts (`.do`) POST form, not a REST/CSV API, but is scriptable (verified via a real POST + response parse in this session).\n\n**Deliberately not pulled further**: this system's 12,008-result scale for Tokyo alone means any real extraction is itself a \\\"collection\\\" decision (how many, which prefecture, what filter) the owner should make explicitly, not something to charge ahead on off a two-word \\\"1, 2\\\" go-ahead. Left as a confirmed-viable, ready-to-use source for a future explicit pull.\n\n## Part 2: canonical id wiring (built)\n\nAdded `crm.dossier-import` (`.cljc`, pure, zero dependency on `cloud-itonami-isic-8291`'s code -- the fleet's \\\"one blueprint = one actor\\\" discipline holds; this only agrees on the DATA SHAPE `dossier.store/company` already returns):\n\n- `dossier-company->account`: keeps a dossier canonical id (`jpn-<corporateNumber>`, `gbr-<company_number>`, ...) verbatim as the 5820 Account's own `:id`, instead of minting a new local `acct-*` id -- the actual DUNS-Number-analog behavior ADR-2607182200 set up the registry for. Refuses a dissolved/malformed/unrecognized-id company outright.\n- **Correctness guard worth naming explicitly**: NEVER sets `:active? true` or invents a `:subscription-tier` for an imported company. On a 5820 Account, `:active?` means \\\"has an active subscription\\\" (`crm.policy/licensed-disclosure-violations`), not \\\"is the legal entity operating\\\" -- those are different facts, and conflating them would silently fabricate customer status for a company that is merely a real, legally-active prospect.\n- `dossier-company->lead`: builds a Lead already account-matched to the canonical id, `:status` always `:new`. Never invents a contact person -- dossier is a company registry, never a people directory (its own ns docstring says so); `name`/`email` are whatever the caller honestly supplies.\n- `crm.store`'s ns docstring documents the `:id` convention (local ad-hoc vs. dossier-canonical) so a future reader doesn't have to reconstruct it from the import module alone.\n\nTests: 87/301 assertions green (was 77/274), clj-kondo clean.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- cloud-itonami now has an end-to-end path from a real, government-verified company (via `dossier.houjin-bangou`, pending the owner's Application ID) to a governed 5820 CRM Account/Lead sharing the SAME id -- no per-actor identity reinvention.\n- Part 1's MHLW source is confirmed and ready; an actual pull (how many agencies, which prefecture(s)) is an explicit follow-up decision, not executed here.\n", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/date "2026-07-18", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607182300: cloud-itonami-isic-5820 dossier-canonical-id wiring + MHLW licensed-agency registry investigation", :adr/source-format "edn"}]